/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  flashSpec01_wet_steam_expansion -- A FLASH SPECIFIED BY A PAIR OTHER THAN
  (T, P) (DEV.md 4c C214 W1; docs/design/a-general-flash-specification.md).

  A state of a fluid of known composition has two degrees of freedom.  The
  isothermal flash fixes them as (T, P); a turbine knows its outlet
  PRESSURE and, ideally, its ENTROPY; a valve knows its pressure and its
  ENTHALPY; a condenser drum knows its pressure and how much of the stream
  is VAPOUR.  Each op below asks one of those pairs of ONE home
  (flashState::specifiedFlash), and every answer is the state the isothermal
  flash publishes there -- except a pure fluid ON its saturation curve,
  where no flash can decide the split and the saturated legs price it.

  THE HAND CHECK (IAPWS-IF97 steam table, per kg):
    expand    80 bar, 500 C:      s = 6.7262 kJ/(kg K), h = 3399.4 kJ/kg
              0.1 bar saturated:  Tsat = 45.81 C, s_f = 0.6492, s_g = 8.1501,
                                  h_f = 191.81, h_g = 2583.9
              quality  x = (6.7262 - 0.6492)/(8.1501 - 0.6492) = 0.8102
              h_out    = 191.81 + 0.8102 (2583.9 - 191.81) = 2129.8 kJ/kg
              isentropic work = 3399.4 - 2129.8 = 1269.6 kJ/kg
    throttle  10 bar, 450 K (subcooled liquid): h = 749.3 kJ/kg
              1 bar saturated:    h_f = 417.4, h_g = 2674.9
              flash fraction x = (749.3 - 417.4)/(2674.9 - 417.4) = 0.147
    halfBoil  1 atm, half vapour: T = Tsat(1 atm) = 373.124 K
    dewP      373.15 K, all vapour: P = Psat(100 C) = 101.418 kPa

  WHAT THE STUDENT WATCHES.  `expand` lands on the saturation PLATEAU: for a
  pure fluid T and P are one condition there, so the state's coordinate is
  the vapour fraction, found by the lever rule on the saturated legs (no
  search).  An isentropic search over a single-phase VAPOUR of fixed
  composition -- what Choupo's turbine does today -- has no root here: below
  s_g at 0.1 bar no vapour carries that entropy (the vapour entropy jumps by
  the whole latent entropy at Tsat), so that search cannot land on this
  answer.  That gap is what this op makes visible.

  NOT MODELLED, said plainly: any non-equilibrium (a real turbine's
  supersaturated "Wilson line" expansion is a kinetic effect); the
  irreversibility of a real expansion (the isentropic state is the ideal
  reference an efficiency is measured against).  No number here is fitted:
  every value is an IF97 evaluation, a STRUCTURAL witness checkable by hand.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
operations
(
    {
        name          expand;
        type          flashSpec;
        composition   { water 1; }
        spec
        {
            pair        PS;
            P           0.1 bar;
            targetFrom  { T 773.15 K;  P 80 bar; }   // the turbine inlet
        }
    }
    {
        name          throttle;
        type          flashSpec;
        composition   { water 1; }
        spec
        {
            pair        PH;
            P           1 bar;
            targetFrom  { T 450 K;  P 10 bar; }      // a subcooled liquid
        }
    }
    {
        name          halfBoil;
        type          flashSpec;
        composition   { water 1; }
        spec
        {
            pair           PVF;
            P              1 atm;
            vaporFraction  0.5;
        }
    }
    {
        name          dewP;
        type          flashSpec;
        composition   { water 1; }
        spec
        {
            pair           TVF;
            T              373.15 K;
            vaporFraction  1;
        }
    }
);
